PasskeyMethodFuzzTest
├── when any key signs a well formed assertion over any digest
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when any key signs with the high half
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when extra members of any length follow the prefix
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when any consistent backup bits accompany user present and user verified
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the assertion carries any signature counter
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the challenge renders any other digest
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when the challenge value carries any extra characters
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when any digest is asserted as webauthn create
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when the assertion names any other relying party
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when any flags byte lacks user present
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when any flags byte lacks user verified
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when any flags byte carries backup state without backup eligibility
│   └── it should answer with one word that is not the verify selector
├── when any other key signs
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when any client data byte changes after signing
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when any authenticator data byte changes after signing
│   └── it should refuse the proof
└── when the config has any length other than ninety six bytes
    └── it should answer with one word that is not the verify selector
